# Every text file is LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Not a style preference. This repository generates files and then checks that
# what is on disk is byte-for-byte what the generator writes — the diagnostics
# registry's drift gate is exactly that comparison, and it is the thing that
# keeps the code table and the files derived from it from drifting apart.
#
# A Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf` on hands that gate CRLF where the
# generator writes LF, so every generated file differs on its first line and the
# gate fires with nothing actually wrong. The fix belongs here rather than in
# the comparison: normalising the comparison would weaken it into "differs only
# in ways we chose to ignore", and the property worth protecting is that the
# file on disk *is* what the generator writes.
#
# `text=auto` leaves git to identify what is text, so binary assets are
# untouched. Nothing in the tree is committed with CRLF today, so this pins the
# state that already exists rather than converting anything.
* text=auto eol=lf
